WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.320
16-ounce bottled water costing under 20 cents wholesale sells for $4 at amusement park stands. This

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:12.400
is First Principles Daily, episode 156. The exclusive contracts that set that stand price,

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:18.000
the material floor under the bottle, the redesigns that could shrink the markup, and the signal

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.240
that the contract itself was the cost. Municipal water sealed in a thin polyethylene

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:30.100
tarathalate bottle, PET, reaches concession stands in bulk cases. The same bottle then carries

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.260
that stand tag once the park gates close behind the customer. Plastic, cap, and water do not explain

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.460
the spread. The contracts that give one vendor soul rights inside a captive audience do.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:47.240
Parks and municipal venues sign long-term exclusive beverage agreements that hand pouring and

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.020
vending rights to a single supplier.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.760
A Dallas City Council memorandum records

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.760
one such 10-year PepsiCo contract covering 66 facilities

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:58.780
and delivering the city more than $1.1 million

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.780
in payments and revenue splits

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.460
in exchange for that exclusivity.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.420
Similar language appears in the Wait Park Amphitheater agreement

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.180
and the Nishoba County Request for Proposals.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.380
Each bar is outside drinks and routes every sale

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.160
through the contracted concessionaire.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.580
Visitors cannot bring their own water

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:21.960
or shop elsewhere once inside, so the vendor faces no direct price competition at the point

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:28.280
of sale. Pennsylvania House Bill, HB 2579, was introduced because those captive conditions

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:34.140
produce markups, legislators, judged excessive. The bill proposes statutory ceilings of $2

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:41.120
for 16 ounces or less, and $4 for 24 ounces or more. Wholesale data from the Baytown Water

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:49.280
Park Bid shows the commodity underneath. 24 bottles of 16.9 ounces sold for $4.44. Roughly

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.060
18.5 cents each. That figure already includes bottling, labeling, and delivery to the park

00:01:55.060 --> 00:02:00.680
operator. The remaining gap sits in contract administration, revenue sharing, and the absence

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:06.300
of alternative sellers, not in any further physical change to the product. Park operators

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:10.440
accept the structure because the exclusivity payment offsets other budget lines

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:16.120
and because every prior operator has done the same. The price feels normal inside the industry

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:20.260
even though the physical object has not changed between the loading dock and the stand.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.440
Liability rules reinforce the pattern. A single vendor simplifies insurance claims and cuts the

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:32.140
number of parties a park must audit for food safety compliance. Revenue splits also push the park

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:37.440
to maximize volume through the exclusive channel, rather than bring in competing sellers that might

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:43.700
erode the payment stream. Over time, the arrangement reinforces itself. Concession staff are trained

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:49.220
only on the contracted product line. Menu boards and refrigeration units are sized and wired

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:54.860
for that supplier's packaging. Wave a magic wand and arrange the atoms instantly into a filled,

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:59.560
capital-caped 60-nouns PET bottle, and three materials dominate the cost.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.640
Commodity PET resin trades at roughly $1 per kilogram.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.400
A typical empty 60-nouns bottle weighs about 20 grams.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:14.140
One kilogram is a thousand grams, so 20 grams is 2% of a kilogram, and 2% of a dollar

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:15.320
is 2 cents of resin.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:18.700
The polypropylene cap adds another cent or two.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:22.260
Treated municipal water is a rounding error at this scale.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:27.360
A few more cents for energy, labels, and basic handling put a rough magic wand

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:32.540
floor between 10 and 15 cents per finished bottle. The Baytown bid already lands

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:37.480
at 18.5 cents delivered. Close to that floor once real logistics are in the

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:42.460
number. Set the stand price of $4 against that floor and the idiot index comes

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:49.600
into view. $4 divided by 15 cents is a bid under 27. $4 divided by 10 cents is

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:54.820
40. Against the delivered wholesale figure, the multiple is lower still, near the bottom

00:03:54.820 --> 00:04:00.860
of that band. The implied index therefore sits roughly between 20 and 40. That ratio does

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:05.620
not come from the plastic or the water. It comes from the sequence of exclusive contracts,

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:11.180
the band on outside beverages, the staffing and permitting overhead of on-site concessions,

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:17.020
and the carrying cost of inventory that competing sellers cannot turn over. Each step multiplies

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.900
the same physical bottle without changing what it is made of.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:23.860
The Pennsylvania Bill's proposed caps acknowledge the same arithmetic.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:29.200
They set maximums only a few times the wholesale number rather than 20 times that number.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:33.800
Because the waste lives in the contractual and regulatory envelope rather than in the

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:38.420
material, shrinking that envelope would move the realized price toward the floor without

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.360
new chemistry or new bottle designs.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:45.600
Transportation from bottling plant to park loading dock is already inside the Baytown

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:50.600
wholesale number, so it cannot explain the further jump of about 20 times at the stand.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:55.720
Refrigeration and shelf space inside the park add only marginal electricity and labor,

00:04:56.260 --> 00:05:01.740
measured in pennies per unit. The dominant multiplier is the contractual barrier that stops any

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:07.309
other seller from offering the identical bottle at a lower margin. A redesign starts by

00:05:07.309 --> 00:05:12.909
separating the physical delivery of bottled water from the exclusivity payment. One concrete move

00:05:12.909 --> 00:05:17.949
is to let visitors carry factory sealed water bought outside the gate. That removes the

00:05:17.949 --> 00:05:23.249
captive audience premium without touching the park's other revenue streams. A second move would

00:05:23.249 --> 00:05:28.769
require concession contracts to publish unit prices and cap the markup at a fixed multiple of

00:05:28.769 --> 00:05:34.689
documented wholesale cost close to the structure floated in the Pennsylvania legislation. A third

00:05:34.689 --> 00:05:40.029
would standardize on one widely available bottle size and resin grade so several suppliers could

00:05:40.029 --> 00:05:44.569
bid the same commodity spec instead of negotiating custom stock keeping units.

00:05:45.069 --> 00:05:50.589
Each step is limited by existing long-term contracts, by insurance and liability rules that

00:05:50.589 --> 00:05:55.589
currently favor single vendor control, and by the administrative cost of watching compliance

00:05:55.589 --> 00:05:56.909
across dozens of venues.

00:05:57.509 --> 00:05:59.269
The prize is visible in the ratio.

00:05:59.809 --> 00:06:05.089
If the idiot index could be driven from 20 plus down to 3 or 4, the same physical bottle

00:06:05.089 --> 00:06:08.989
would reach the customer at something closer to $0.75 instead of $4.

00:06:08.989 --> 00:06:13.409
dollars, while still covering the supplier's documented costs and a reasonable margin.

00:06:13.929 --> 00:06:19.249
A fourth step could put mobile refill stations on site, treating municipal water and dispensing

00:06:19.249 --> 00:06:20.709
it into reusable containers.

00:06:21.269 --> 00:06:25.209
That would still have to solve hygiene verification and queue management at scale.

00:06:25.829 --> 00:06:28.769
The hardest constraint remains the multi-year contract cycle.

00:06:29.349 --> 00:06:33.389
Any change would need to be negotiated at renewal rather than imposed midterm.

00:06:34.341 --> 00:06:38.841
When a simple commodity travels through an exclusive gate, the contract itself becomes

00:06:38.841 --> 00:06:44.181
the dominant cost component. The bottle does not get heavier, pure, or harder to make between

00:06:44.181 --> 00:06:49.061
the dock and the stand. What changes is who is allowed to sell it, and what the venue is paid

00:06:49.061 --> 00:06:55.101
for keeping everyone else out. Dallas traded a decade of pouring rights across 66 facilities for

00:06:55.101 --> 00:07:00.301
more than a million dollars in payments and splits. Weight Park in Nishoba wrote the same kind

00:07:00.301 --> 00:07:06.101
of bar on outside drinks. Those payments are real money for a city budget. They are also a toll

00:07:06.101 --> 00:07:10.801
collected, bottled by bottle, from people who cannot walk back out and buy the identical

00:07:10.801 --> 00:07:12.641
PET container somewhere else.

00:07:13.141 --> 00:07:18.341
Remove that gate or cap its toll at a modest multiple of delivered cost, and the physical

00:07:18.341 --> 00:07:20.481
floor reappears as a practical price.

00:07:21.161 --> 00:07:23.961
The Magic Wand estimate already says the atoms are cheap.

00:07:24.581 --> 00:07:29.261
The Baytown invoice already says a real supplier can land the finished bottle near that floor.

00:07:29.861 --> 00:07:30.841
Logistics included.

00:07:31.381 --> 00:07:34.941
What keeps the stand price far above both is not a missing invention.

00:07:34.941 --> 00:07:40.601
It is a rule renewed on a calendar that treats a commodity as if it were a unique service.

00:07:41.141 --> 00:07:44.561
Tomorrow and every day after, one example or one opportunity.

00:07:45.141 --> 00:07:49.261
The first signal that someone is testing this path would be a venue that publishes both

00:07:49.261 --> 00:07:52.461
its wholesale invoice and its stand price side-by-side.

00:07:52.841 --> 00:07:55.481
That's a wrap on today's first principles breakdown.

00:07:56.181 --> 00:07:58.601
The ideas travel further when you pass them on.

00:07:59.121 --> 00:08:01.921
Send this to a fellow builder, I'm Patrick and Vancouver.

